1
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,910
What happened?

2
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:23,940
The baby-sitter called.

3
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,430
His daughter is sick.

4
00:00:26,430 --> 00:00:28,060
What's wrong?

5
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:32,360
I think she has a stomachache.

6
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:37,140
He's a good father.

7
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:41,190
So... what do you think of him?

8
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:43,220
He's very nice.

9
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:45,860
But I think he was nervous tonight.

10
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:51,570
It was his first date in two years.

11
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:53,510
Will you see him again?

12
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:58,010
I hope so.

13
00:00:58,010 --> 00:01:01,960
This food is delicious.

14
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:04,310
He didn't get a thing to eat.

15
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:06,870
You ordered enough for three or four people,

16
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:08,870
but I'm not complaining.

17
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:12,580
The food is delicious.

18
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,290
Who is that?

19
00:01:14,290 --> 00:01:15,800
Do you think it's...

20
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:24,720
No. You won't believe it, Marilyn!

21
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:29,970
I believe it. Even without looking.

22
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:31,140
Hi!

23
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:31,960
How...?

24
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:35,100
Your downstairs neighbor let me in.

25
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:36,170
Did you go home?

26
00:01:36,170 --> 00:01:37,710
I did , but everything is OK,

27
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:40,510
so I decided to come back.

28
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:43,000
To apologize for leaving so early,

29
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,240
I brought you a little gift.

30
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:45,960
It's a bonsai tree

31
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,020
for your new apartment.

32
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,240
Hi, Marilyn. I hope it's not too late.

33
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,730
Oh, not at all. We're still eating.

34
00:01:52,730 --> 00:01:55,890
Please, come in. Join us.

35
00:01:55,890 --> 00:01:59,460
It's our meal from the restaurant.

36
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,540
And how is your daughter?

37
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,300
Oh, she's fine.

38
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,310
It was only a tummy ache.

39
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:06,420
It's good that you went back.

40
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:09,850
Yes, I think it's important for me to be there

41
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:11,640
since her mother died.

42
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:16,330
I agree. Aren't you hungry?

43
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:19,900
As a matter of fact... I am hungry.

44
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,850
There's lots of food left.

45
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:25,460
Mmm, this is delicious!

46
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:26,900
Enjoy!

47
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,030
I'm going to excuse myself.

48
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:33,070
I have a lot of work to do to get ready for tomorrow.

49
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,810
Good night, Harry. It was nice meeting you.

50
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:36,040
Bye, Marilyn.

51
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:37,320
Good night, Susan.

52
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:40,770
Good night, Marilyn.

53
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:43,860
She's going to a fashion show here in the city tomorrow.

54
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:45,260
She is sleeping here

55
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:48,270
so she won't have to travel from Riverdale in the morning.

56
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:50,960
You two must be close.

57
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:52,140
we are.

58
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:55,470
The whole Stewart family is close.

59
00:02:55,470 --> 00:03:06,640
I like that.

60
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:10,630
And then, two years ago, my wife died.

61
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:13,060
You miss her.

62
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,810
I do...yes, but I have Michelle...

63
00:03:15,810 --> 00:03:20,290
and with time...

64
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:24,070
Is there anyone else in your life?

65
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:29,620
No, not yet. What about you?

66
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,670
Oh, I date occasionally,

67
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:34,130
but my work keeps me busy.

68
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,210
Ooh, speaking of keeping busy-

69
00:03:36,210 --> 00:03:37,630
I have an early start tomorrow,

70
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:41,220
and the baby-sitter has to get home.

71
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:43,050
Where did the time go?

72
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:48,960
It's midnight.

73
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,160
Thank you, Susan.

74
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:52,770
I had a nice evening.

75
00:03:52,770 --> 00:04:02,230
Me, too, Harry.

76
00:04:02,230 --> 00:04:03,920
Harry?

77
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:05,510
Yes?

78
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:09,320
I'd like to meet your daughter someday.

79
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:12,070
Does that mean that I can see you again?

80
00:04:12,070 --> 00:04:13,140
Of course.

81
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:14,930
Wonderful. I'll call you,

82
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:16,160
and we'll go out to dinner.

83
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:16,850
Please do.

84
00:04:16,850 --> 00:04:19,150
I promise I won't leave early.

85
00:04:19,150 --> 00:04:22,250
It was for a good reason.

86
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:24,360
You know something?

87
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,340
What?

88
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:28,880
I think we're going to be good friends.

89
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:30,070
Good night, Susan.

90
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:31,600
Good night, Harry,

91
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:41,850
Have a safe trip home.

92
00:04:41,850 --> 00:04:44,340
Are you all right?

93
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:46,380
Sorry.

94
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:51,170
I never liked that umbrella stand.

95
00:04:51,170 --> 00:04:54,170
Good night, Harry.
